WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Two things to settle before you build.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:03.688
First, where it runs.

3
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:07.049
There's no FedRAMP package
for CyberArk's cloud edition,

4
00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:11.652
so the program runs the self-hosted
edition inside the agency's own boundary,

5
00:00:11.652 --> 00:00:14.575
next to the certificate
authorities it manages.

6
00:00:14.575 --> 00:00:18.873
Second, what it runs on: Windows
servers, English-language builds,

7
00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:24.063
all on the same version, with a SQL Server
database that lives on its own server.

8
00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:26.830
Plan for an upgrade
roughly every six months,

9
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.374
because that's CyberArk's release rhythm.

10
00:00:29.374 --> 00:00:31.400
The full requirements are on the slide.

11
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.640
Next, let's open the box and see what
the platform is actually made of.
